ttps://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T17:28:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T17:28:26Z","body":"Fixed styling, created documentation and removed random white spaces. I think it should be ready now.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729899003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729936549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3729936549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3729936549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eUlCl","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T17:40:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T17:43:16Z","body":"i think an exposed `bool mouse_picking = false;` would be desired and be set to false as default, because of performance and to allow some modality to the user to enable/disable this behaviour without additional boilerplate.\r\n\r\nAdditionally the use if input means that any input that was previously handled will be ignored, this means _gui_input and _input could cause strange states because the propagation will stop before reaching this object and not emmit properly the signals when the user may be expecting them to\r\n\r\nThis code also assumes the existence of said signals, but they dont exists to any other class. They could probably be moved to CanvasItem.\r\nmake a virtual call to `_has_point()` like happens in Control, and mention the possibility to implement this method on any CanvasItem","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729936549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729991714","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3729991714","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3729991714,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eUygi","user":{"login":"Ezequias-Rodrigues","id":7608708,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDg3MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7608708?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues","html_url":"https://github.com/Ezequias-Rodrigues","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T17:58:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T17:58:49Z","body":"I'll implement this \"mouse_picking\", good idea.\r\n\r\nI think i don't quite understand what you mean in your second point. Isn't it expected that the input is \"consumed\", and ignored if it was already \"consumed\" by something up in the propagation path? (English is not my mother tongue, sorry)\r\n\r\nThe signals exists in control, i can \"bring them up\", which i haven't done yet because it may cause some unexpected behavior, or i can rename and put them at canvas item, something like \"cursor_entered/exited/pressed\". I'm accepting suggestions.\r\n\r\nAbout the _has_point: will do.\r\nThanks for your feedback ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729991714/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730056070","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3730056070","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3730056070,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eVCOG","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T18:18:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T18:25:36Z","body":"The second point is related to the [order in which inputs are propagated in the engine](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/inputs/inputevent.html#how-does-it-work) (however i was mistakenly beliving _gui_input was happening before _input)\r\n\r\nIf your Sprite captures mouse_enter, and then another Sprite captures the MouseMotion because you entered it, that was ment to cause the mouse_exit, and you click the mouse, then the Engine will still believe the mouse is inside the first sprite and not call mouse_exited. Also the order of propagation of `_input` is from top to bottom (in the scene tree) meaning that the node that has priority to set the input as handled is the one drawn behind, not in the top\r\n\r\nAll of this complex interactions is the reason why mouse picking was considered exclusive to Controls, _gui_input is processed from bottom to top, meaning the node that handles the input will be the one drawn last, and also viewport keeps internal state related to the last hovered Control to mark it as unhovered when another control takes that place\r\n\r\nA simple workaround to mouse enter/exit in sprites is useing a TextureRect and override _has_point(local_position) to check the texture pixel and return color.a > 0.01\r\n\r\nPolygon2D requires to override _input tho","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730056070/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730398403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3730398403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3730398403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eWVzD","user":{"login":"Ezequias-Rodrigues","id":7608708,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDg3MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7608708?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues","html_url":"https://github.com/Ezequias-Rodrigues","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ezequias-Rodrigues/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T20:02:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T20:07:05Z","body":"Ok about the second point, i think that i'll have to make the change from scene_tree(so, my initial idea was not that far off, i should've tried that first instead of going for canvasitem)\r\n\r\nIn line 1435 in scene_tree.cpp, there's a loop that iterate over all the nodes, from the last to the first(if i got this correctly). So, i think that i should use scene_tree to keep track of which node is being focused(like viewport for Controls elements), and \"intercept\" the input in this iteration, which already exists so it shouldn't have much of a performance impact. This then should respect the priority order and, if i implement the tracking correctly, avoid the situation that you've described. \r\nIs this logic sound? I'm still familiarizing myself with the engine source, so sorry if this seems kinda of a newbie question.\r\n\r\nAbout the workarounds the sprite2D kinda of does that in _mouse_hit_test(i'll refactor it to _has_point for better clarity). \r\n\r\n_Note: Please correct me if i got anything wrong. I don't understand why the function the said loop is called_ _call_input_pause, _but it seems that it is the one where the input propagation starts from._\r\n ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730398403/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730961581","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3730961581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3730961581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eYfSt","user":{"login":"MarianoGnu","id":1776044,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NzYwNDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1776044?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu","html_url":"https://github.com/MarianoGnu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MarianoGnu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T23:25:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T23:26:32Z","body":"as i pointed out, the same input is propagated several times trugh the game\r\nfirst `_input` from top to bottom\r\nthen `_gui_input` from bottom to top, and only Control(s)\r\nthen `_shortcut_input` (i'm unaware of the order of this, and if is exclusive to controls, but doesn't matter in your case because only propagates keyboard inputs)\r\nthen `_unhandled_key_input` (again unaware of the order, but is still keyboard inputs\r\nthen `_unhandled_input` all nodes from top to bottom, this is a second chance to catch an input if wasn't handled previously\r\nthen and only then, Physics checks for mouse events, i think this happens always, no matter if event was handled or not\r\n\r\nSo, i dont know which one of all those events is the loop you are seeing in scene_tree, or maybe is all of them\r\n\r\nthis is all much better explained [in the documentation](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/inputs/inputevent.html#how-does-it-work)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730961581/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750719020","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3750719020","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3750719020,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fj24s","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T17:29:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T17:29:57Z","body":"Please do not push so many times in a row, you are a first time contributor so you need approval to run CI, but otherwise this would really take up a lot of CI processing and time, so please make your changes in a batch","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750719020/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750776823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114776#issuecomment-3750776823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114776","id":3750776823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7fkE_3","user":{"login":"Ezequias-Rodrigues","id":7608708,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDg3MDg=","